<title>PERU: Peru's August wheat production dips 6.5 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's August wheat production dips 6.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's August wheat production fell 6.5 percent to 14,112 tonnes from the same month last year, Agriculture Ministry said Wednesday.</p>
<p>However, output for the first eight months was up 26.8 percent at 123,151 tonnes compared to the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Total 1995 wheat production was 125,048 tonnes.</p>
<p>Wheat imports in August rose 16.9 percent to 19.653 tonnes, worth $21.656 million, while in the first eight months imports rose 43.1 percent to 154,835 tonnes, worth $171.295 million.</p>
<p>Peru's wheat is grown mostly in the central and southeastern Andean regions.</p>
<p>--Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
